<details class="optional" id="decisions"><summary>Implementation decisions</summary>
<p>The core deliberately favors explicit code: Java 21, supported Spring Boot, Maven Wrapper, JdbcClient/SQL, Thymeleaf and Flyway; Python 3.12, direct Azure SDK clients and small HTTP model calls; PostgreSQL 17 and an exact pgvector cosine scan. Application source is maintained in {{repo:products}}, {{repo:embedder}} and {{repo:chat}}. The two Python repositories vendor the same small rag_core package; the integration checks compare them.</p>
<p>PostgreSQL is private to the VNet, with a delegated subnet and private DNS. AKS and Functions use explicit NAT egress for public, identity-protected Azure endpoints. Storage containers are private and shared-key access is disabled. This core avoids private endpoints for every service and avoids a multi-day network/security course.</p>
<p>One database owner is used by migrations and applications, and TLS <code>sslmode=require</code> encrypts PostgreSQL traffic inside the private network. Production should separate runtime/migration roles and use full certificate/hostname verification appropriate to its trust store. The Products endpoint has self-signed HTTPS, a source-IP restriction and a random password. It is not public anonymous HTTP, nor a production SSO implementation.</p>
<p>Application settings/secrets are read only on startup. Workers are serial with prefetch zero. Messaging is at-least-once with explicit idempotency. Model calls have finite connect/read timeouts; request deadlines and failure states persist independently of the browser.</p>
</details>
