<details class="optional" id="costs"><summary>Cost drivers and cleanup</summary>
<p>The four-hour US$5–15 planning allowance is intentionally approximate. It assumes one small node, a Burstable database, a few manuals, at most a handful of bounded eight-question demos, and prompt deletion. No bill has been measured for this implementation. Regional capacity, pricing agreements, minimum billing units and model token usage change the result.</p>
<ul><li><strong>Persistent until deletion:</strong> AKS node/disks, database compute/storage, NAT/public IPs, ACR, Service Bus and App Configuration. Scaling the chat worker to zero does not remove these costs.</li><li><strong>Usage-based:</strong> model tokens, Function execution, storage operations/data transfer and log ingestion. Restrict repeated load runs; failed/retried model calls can also cost tokens.</li><li><strong>After cleanup:</strong> confirm ARM deletion and AKS's node-group removal. Soft-deleted Key Vault/App Configuration names remain subject to their recovery/retention behavior.</li></ul>
<p>Use <a href="https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/pricing/calculator/">Azure Pricing Calculator</a>, <a href="https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/pricing/details/kubernetes-service/">AKS pricing</a>, <a href="https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/pricing/details/postgresql/flexible-server/">PostgreSQL pricing</a> and <a href="https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/pricing/details/cognitive-services/openai-service/">Azure model pricing</a> before your own run. Budget alerts notify; they are not a hard spending cap.</p>
</details>
